  "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'someone get me the goddamn tranny mulcher', which uses the first-person plural 'someone' and the imperative 'get me' to create a direct, personal demand. This implies the user is identifying with the speaker of the demand, projecting themselves into the role of the person who is violently demanding the destruction of transgender people. The projection is onto the textual material, which contains the explicit deictic 'me', making the user feel personally implicated in the hateful act described.",
